  "question": "A rental company needs to manage customer credit records. Customers have name, phone number, and credit score. Each rental needs to record rental time, return time, and rental fee. The company needs to track changes in customer credit, with each record including change time, change reason, old credit value, and new credit value, to facilitate credit assessment and performance evaluation.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0067\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `credit_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `rentals` (\n  `rental_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rental_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `return_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rental_fee` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`rental_id`),\n  KEY `rentals_ibfk_1` (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `rentals_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer_credit_changes` (\n  `change_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `change_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `change_reason` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `old_credit_value` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `new_credit_value` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`change_id`),\n  KEY `customer_credit_changes_ibfk_1` (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `customer_credit_changes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
